# HP48gII full stock launch: stock Kermit -> ARMToolbox48 -> hpclang HPC1.
2000 tap f6
4000 tap f6
# Factory default is ALG; use RPN for the stack-based library install.
5000 tap mode
5500 tap neg
6000 tap f6
7000 capture home-rpn
# Configure wire I/O to Serial.
8000 tap files
9500 tap down
10000 tap enter
11500 tap down
12000 tap down
12500 tap down
13000 tap down
14000 tap enter
16000 tap up
17000 tap f2
18000 tap down
18500 tap enter
20000 tap enter
# Start stock Kermit server.
22000 tap files
23500 tap down
24500 tap enter
26000 tap down
27000 tap down
28000 tap down
29000 tap down
30000 tap down
31500 tap enter
33500 capture server-serial
# Host begins Kermit at t=35s and has a 70s transfer timeout. Do not resume
# calculator UI automation before t=105s: a successful 62s transfer previously
# finished at t=97s and raced the old t=95s VAR sequence.
110000 capture after-transfer
# Install ARMToolbox48 Library 275 into Port 0. With both variables present,
# HPCLANG is F1 and L275 is F2 in the HOME VAR menu.
111000 tap var
112000 capture vars-before-install
113000 tap f2
114000 capture l275-stack
115000 tap zero
116000 tap enter
117000 capture port-zero-stack
118000 tap sto
120000 capture stored
122000 chord on f3
128000 capture after-warmstart
# L275 moved to Port 0; HPCLANG remains the first HOME variable.
129000 tap var
130000 capture vars-after-install
131000 tap f1
133000 capture hpclang-stack
# Library 275 is the first LIB entry; ARMTo exposes PrRUN on F1.
135000 chord rshift two
136500 capture lib-menu
137500 tap f1
139000 capture armtoolbox
140000 tap f1
143000 monitor 60000
